  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping study on the informal waste sector in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this study is to analyse the informal economy in the waste management sector in Ghaziabad, Mumbai, Muzaffarnagar and Nagpur and identify interventions that will lead to improved labour conditions, and ultimately formalisation of informal waste workers.With the combi-track, the Dutch government aims to improve the income and working conditions of informal workers in the value chain, such as waste pickers and waste collectors, with a focus on women and youth.The study is conducted specifically for the combi-track and the results will therefore also be for use in the combi-track Waste. Following the study, the Dutch government will be able to determine what interventions are required to make a positive impact on the informal waste sector, in above-mentioned locations in India, and which of these interventions could be provided by the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
